WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.940
Gregor Mendel’s experiments laid the foundation

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.180
of modern day Genetics.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.540
We have seen so far that Mendel crossed a

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.960
purple flowered plant with a white flowered

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.740
plant.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.480
He then collected the seeds and grew new plants

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:19.980
from them.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.900
Astonishingly, he found that all the offsprings

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.900
had purple coloured flowers.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.857
Now, on crossing these plants among themselves,

00:00:29.857 --> 00:00:32.750
Mendel surprisingly obtained three purple

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.620
flowered plants and one white flowered plant.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.180
How could this be possible?

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.200
Moreover, what could be the probable reasons for this?

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:45.720
The first set of results were that all the

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.820
plants in the first or F one generation were

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.140
with purple coloured flowers.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.380
Here, the term “F1” indicates the FIRST

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.720
FILIAL generation.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.340
In this case, he considered Colour of the

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.660
flower as a character.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.200
Did he cross pea plants having other characters too?

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.880
Yes! he considered ALL the other characters

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.280
like plant height, seed colour and so on.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.080
And then he found that only ONE character

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.360
is expressed in the F1 generation.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.240
For instance, he crossed a pea plant having

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.240
round seeds with the one having wrinkled seeds.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.700
In the F1 generation, he obtained all the

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.920
plants having ONLY ROUND seeds.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.240
It implied that the offsprings are similar

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.200
to ONLY ONE of the parents and do not have

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.440
any resemblance with the other ! And this

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.500
was seen for all the characters!

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.660
Now getting back to our example of flower colour…

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.240
Mendel obtained all the plants with purple

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.700
coloured flowers in the F1 generation.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.080
But this wasn’t the case in the next step

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.360
When the offsprings from this F1 generation

00:01:58.369 --> 00:02:01.410
were crossed, one plant out of the four had

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:04.310
traits just like the original parent that

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.660
was considered.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.659
That means in this case, one out of the four

00:02:09.659 --> 00:02:12.969
had white coloured flowers and three had purple

00:02:12.969 --> 00:02:14.100
coloured flowers.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.940
With this, he concluded that characters are

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.560
passed from one generation to the other.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.340
With the current knowledge we have, we know

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.540
that this is due to the passing of genes.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.960
However, it was not known back then.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.980
Mendel named these as “factors”.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.955
So it was believed that there are “factors”

00:02:34.955 --> 00:02:37.989
which carry these traits from one generation

00:02:37.989 --> 00:02:39.020
to the other.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.553
But what about the disappearance of the trait

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.109
in one complete generation?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.315
In the F1 generation, the trait of white coloured

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.540
flowers was not seen at all.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.600
This was explained by Mendel in a very efficient manner.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.340
He explained that in organisms like the green

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.520
peas, one “FACTOR ” is always expressed

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:04.780
and it super powers the presence of the OTHER “factor”.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.840
We call these factors as “genes” or “alleles” now.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.957
We will have a detailed look at what genes

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.660
mean in our upcoming parts.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.240
But,for now, let us focus on Mendel’s work.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.180
In today’s terms, Mendel said that some

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.880
genes are always expressed irrespective of

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:25.840
the other.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.760
These are called Dominant genes . The others

00:03:29.766 --> 00:03:32.859
which are suppressed are referred to as recessive

00:03:32.859 --> 00:03:33.359
genes .

00:03:33.359 --> 00:03:37.299
So why did the recessive genes not express

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.460
themselves in the F1 generation?

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.660
And how did they get expressed in the F2 generation?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.780
Let's understand this with the help of a

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.140
theoretical explanation of this cross.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:53.280
Let's consider letter “P” written in

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.569
upper case as the allele, that is “factor”

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.300
in Mendel’s terms, for the purple coloured flower.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.100
And the white coloured flower will be represented

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.159
with the allele “p” written in lower case.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:10.100
Now, the first cross included purple flowered

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.440
plant and a white flowered plant.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:16.000
So this is how we can represent this crossing.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.480
Any idea why have we used the letter “P” twice here?

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.020
It’s simple!

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.560
The Green pea plant is a diploid plant.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.980
What does “diploid” mean?

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.640
We have always come across the saying that

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.180
humans have “23 PAIRS” of chromosomes…

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.860
That’s because the chromosomes in us are

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.240
always in pairs.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.080
Each set has one chromosome from each parent.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.060
This is nothing but the diploid nature.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.820
So when organisms have two sets of chromosomes,

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:53.140
they are referred to as “diploid” organisms.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.640
Getting back to green peas, there are two

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:58.720
sets of genes in it.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.560
That is why we use the letter twice to represent

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.460
both the allelic forms.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:08.360
So here, “PP” written in upper case will

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.220
represent the purple colour of flowers, while

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.960
“pp” written in lower case will represent

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.140
the white colour of flowers!

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.700
Now in this cross, the gametes, which are

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:22.220
nothing but the reproductive cells, will be

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.820
formed like this… and the cross will yield

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:26.820
us this result.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.180
How?

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.680
This combination, this one, then this one

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.280
and this is the last one!

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.220
These are the 4 possible combinations.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.360
Now, as you can see here, “Pp” indicates

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.700
that the offspring has one dominant and one

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.320
recessive allele.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.600
In such a case, the plants will have only

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.660
purple flowers, as the presence of one dominant

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.580
gene is enough to express the trait.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:59.120
That is the reason why ALL the plants have

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.640
purple coloured flowers in the F1 generation.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.880
Now, can you guess why the ratio “three

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.180
to one” is obtained in the F2 generation?

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.760
Let's find that out with the help of a similar

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.980
theoretical cross.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:18.020
Here, we take any two random plants from the

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.140
F1 generation.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.600
Crossing these two or even by carrying out

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.220
the selfing process in a similar fashion gives

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:27.160
us this result.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:32.140
Now, as we can see here, these three offsprings

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:33.980
have at least one dominant gene.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.000
That is the reason why each of these is a

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.140
purple flowered plant.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.580
Now in this case, both the genes are recessive:

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.460
that means no gene to dominate the trait.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:49.260
As a result, the plant expresses the recessive

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.700
trait that is white coloured flowers.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.400
This was the simplest way to explain Mendel’s results.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.680
Dominant genes are those which are expressed

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.860
in both: homozygous and heterozygous forms.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:06.600
On the other hand, recessive genes are those

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:09.000
which can be expressed only when present in

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.420
homozygous form.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.280
Hold on…

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.060
Any idea, what we mean by Homozygous and

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.400
Heterozygous?

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.940
We know that the term “homo ” means same

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.660
and “hetero ” means different.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:28.100
So Homozygous means the set of genes are same

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.940
: both either dominant or both recessive.

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:35.620
For example, “PP” and “pp” are both

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.100
homozygous forms.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.920
Heterozygous is exactly opposite of this!

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.460
It simply means both the forms are different.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:48.160
So here, “Pp” represents the heterozygous

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.180
form: one dominant and one recessive!

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:55.460
So, the dominant alleles are expressed in

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:59.600
both homozygous and heterozygous forms, while

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.800
recessive alleles can be expressed when present

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.100
only in the homozygous forms!

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.920
This was just an introduction to Mendel’s experiments.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.160
Let's have a look at one more example and

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.280
a few more terms in genetics in the next part!

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.820
We have seen how the cross of a character

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.500
like flower colour is carried out.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.860
In this part, let's get introduced to a few

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.960
more interesting terms in genetics.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.920
But, before that, let's understand the cross

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.980
of one more character and get thorough with

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:38.920
it!

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.440
Before beginning any such experiment, we need

00:08:42.443 --> 00:08:44.920
to make sure that the parents selected are

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:46.420
Homozygous in nature.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:51.140
So let’s say, we wish to cross two organisms

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.280
with some trait named “A”.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:57.480
The dominant form should ideally be “AA”

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.600
both in upper case, while the recessive form

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.720
has to be “aa” both in lower case.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:08.600
Now, the recessive form will definitely be homozygous.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:09.880
Why?

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.940
Yes, we know that the recessive character

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:16.000
is expressed only when it is in the homozygous

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:16.920
form.

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:20.160
But the dominant character can have both the

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.340
set of alleles.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.431
So, “AA” in upper case as well as “Aa”

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:29.500
one in upper and the other in lower case,

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.570
can give us a dominant case.

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:35.779
So, it could be homozygous or heterozygous.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.460
Now, how are we supposed to know whether the

00:09:39.465 --> 00:09:43.319
organism considered for crossing is homozygous

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:46.509
or heterozygous for a particular character?

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:50.520
For this, we have the concept of pure lines

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.100
Pure lines are nothing but the descendants

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:57.560
obtained after inbreeding for several generations

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.460
Confused? Don’t be!

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:03.700
It’s easy to understand this with an example.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.680
Let’s say we have this particular breed

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:07.840
of dogs.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:11.100
Both these have genes for a good coat on their

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:12.160
skin, say “C”.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:16.260
So, both these dogs may have the genes “CC”

00:10:16.271 --> 00:10:19.319
both in upper case or “Cc” that is, one

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.600
in upper and the other in lower case.

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:26.040
On crossing these two dogs, we get these offsprings.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:30.959
Clearly, the genes are passed to this generation.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:34.371
Now, on crossing any of the two dogs from

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:37.460
this same progeny, we get these offsprings.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:40.440
That means again, the same set of genes is

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:42.220
passed to the next generation.

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:46.480
Imagine, this is done for a few more generations.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.280
What will be the result?

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.280
The progeny at the end will have these genes

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:52.120
conserved.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.080
But notice something interesting!

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.340
As we keep crossing the individuals in the

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.880
same family, the chances of obtaining the

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:03.700
homozygous form is enhanced.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.320
This process of crossing individuals from

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:10.940
the same family is called inbreeding . And

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:14.000
offsprings obtained after inbreeding several

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.140
generations are called pure lines .

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.140
One of the advantages of using pure lines

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:22.640
while beginning the experiment is to have

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:25.884
an assurance that the organism is HOMOZYGOUS

00:11:25.884 --> 00:11:28.160
even for the dominant trait.

00:11:28.940 --> 00:11:31.760
Now, let's focus back on the cross we were

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:32.920
about to carry out!

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.180
This time, let's consider the character “Stem

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:37.420
Height ” in the pea plant.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:41.300
Here, we take a tall and a dwarf plant.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.840
Both these are pure lines.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.440
On crossing the Parental generation, we get

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:51.500
these offsprings in the F1 generation.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:55.100
Now, what will happen when we cross these

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.160
two plants from the F1 generation?

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:59.860
It will give us these results.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:02.480
Take a moment to go through this.

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:08.399
So what we get is three tall plants and one dwarf plant.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:11.740
Isn’t this the same ratio that Mendel obtained

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:15.020
when flower colour was considered as the character?

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:16.860
Yes it is!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.340
He had obtained three purple and one white

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.080
flower in the F2 generation.

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:27.240
Similarly, here we get three tall and one dwarf plant!

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:31.240
Now that we have had a good idea about crossing,

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.820
let me introduce 2 new terms to you…

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.339
Trust me they are very simple to understand!

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:42.959
The two terms are phenotypic ratio and genotypic ratio!

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:47.620
In this case , the phenotypic ratio is three to one.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:50.860
That is three tall plants and one dwarf plant!

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:55.280
And the genotypic ratio is one to two to one.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.400
As we can see, one plant is homozygous for

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:02.140
the tall trait, these two are heterozygous

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:04.860
and this one is homozygous for the recessive

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.140
trait, dwarf!

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.759
Any idea, what these terms mean?

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:13.359
Let's understand them first and then proceed

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.100
with understanding the ratios!

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:18.920
The features that can be seen or observed

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:21.240
by us externally are called “phenotypes”.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.740
Pheno is a prefix that indicates an OBSERVABLE

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.000
characteristic!

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:31.360
We could clearly see in this case, three are

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:33.280
tall and one is a dwarf plant.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:37.600
Hence, the phenotypic ratio is three to one.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.780
What about the genotypic ratio?

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.360
Let’s take an example here!

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:46.700
If we look at this tall guy, what can we say

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.020
about his genes?

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.700
This tall guy can have the genes ‘TT’

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.380
both in uppercase, or ‘Tt’ one in upper

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:56.999
and the other in lower case!

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.340
We can’t really predict it!

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:03.560
So just by having a GLANCE, we can’t really

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:07.240
guess if the individual is homozygous or heterozygous

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.480
for height as the character.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:13.660
So the features at the genetic level, which

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.080
cannot be observed, are called “genotypes

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:20.080
”.
In simple words, the physical expression of

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:23.620
the genes, giving rise to the particular observable

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.600
traits can be termed as “phenotype”.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:30.200
On the other hand, genotype can be defined

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:33.080
as the set of genes that give rise to a particular

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:37.840
trait : That is the genetic makeup of an organism!

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:41.312
So, the trait that's visible to us is the

00:14:41.312 --> 00:14:44.429
phenotype and what genes the organism has

00:14:44.429 --> 00:14:46.920
for that trait, is the genotype.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.800
For example, if this boy has black eyes, then

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:54.060
the eye colour seen by us is the boy’s phenotype,

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:57.180
and the genes that he has inherited from his

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:00.040
parents, which are not seen by us are a part

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:01.880
of his genotype!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.260
Now getting back to our experiment…

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:08.680
How do we understand the genotypic ratio?

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:12.759
Well, as we can see, we have one homozygous

00:15:12.759 --> 00:15:16.459
tall plant, two heterozygous tall plants,

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:19.420
and one homozygous dwarf plant.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:24.220
So, the genotypic ratio is one to two to one.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.120
Now, we are well versed with the crosses and

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.840
also a few important terms in genetics.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:34.060
Take a moment to go through these important

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:34.840
terms once!

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:40.600
Let's now move ahead and understand Gregor

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.800
Mendel’s experiments further.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.440
So far, we have seen how Mendel crossed plants

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:50.180
and studied one character at a time . Do you

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:52.640
think he always crossed only a single character

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:53.860
at a time?

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:55.320
No

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:58.680
After he completed crossing all the characters

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:01.500
individually, he crossed two characters at

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:04.300
a time, followed by three and so on!

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.020
The cross involving one character at a time

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:11.680
is called Monohybrid cross . So, whatever

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:14.320
we have learnt so far was a Monohybrid cross.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.760
And the ratio obtained after the cross is

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.180
nothing but a Monohybrid ratio.

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:24.500
How is a Dihybrid cross that is a cross involving

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:27.240
two characters at a time carried out then?

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.200
And what about the Dihybrid ratio?

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:33.840
Let's get to know that in the next part!

